# What must never be sent to the Docker daemon as build context.
#
# Two reasons: secrets (a .env read into an image layer would be readable by anyone who can
# pull it) and size (target/ and uploads/ are hundreds of megabytes and would be copied over
# on every build, on a 2 GB server).

# Secrets — the build needs none of these, and the Dockerfile copies only pom.xml and src/.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build output: the image builds the jar itself, from source.
target/

# Uploaded stadium photos: they live on a named volume, never in the image.
uploads/

# Git history and local tooling.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.idea
.vscode
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar

# JVM crash dumps and logs that happen to be lying around.
*.log
hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*

# Documentation, Postman collections and the deploy files: none are compiled into the jar.
# deploy/ is excluded on purpose — docker-compose.yml reads it from the host, not the image.
*.md
docs/
postman/
scripts/
deploy/
